            "review_title": "Review at La Phong Sushi House",
            "review_text": "Kelvin\nSingapore, Singapore16 contributions\n0\nHorrible & Overpriced Food - NOT Fresh at All!\nDec 2015 • Couples\nWe were initially heading to Sushi Rei (few hundred meters from this place) but was told by the chef that it was full for the night. Pulled up La Phong from TripAdvisor and saw pretty stellar reviews - thought, hey, why not?\n\nWorst. Meal. Ever.\n\nTo give some context, my girlfriend and I are actually avid Japanese foodies - we have at least 3 to 4 Japanese meals a week, in our home country and also abroad, and La Phong truly takes the cake for being the worst ever meal. Oh, and she puked after the meal, in the washroom, too.\n\n1) Wrong order of dishes: For a fine-dining Japanese restaurant at over 1,000,000 VND (50 USD+) per pax, you would think they could serve the right dishes in the right order. Nope, apparently that's rocket science to them! Also, they bombarded the table with so many dishes at once that it had to be placed outside of the table mat.\n\n2) The chefs are.. incompetent - ingredients are not fresh at all! The ikura (salmon roe) used was slimy and slightly hardened - a sign that it was left for days, probably not at the right temperature, or cured incorrectly. The chef also ruined a perfectly nice cut of fatty tuna belly but slicing it incorrectly.\n\n3) The clearing of dishes before it's even done: Maybe the staff are a little too enthusiastic, but they kept prompting whether we were done with the dishes to clear the plate. Most of the times, we were still chewing the food and poof, the plate was gone already.\n\n4) The set selection spread: To be honest, the items weren't specified beforehand (moriwase), but one would expect that the most expensive set on the menu be at least decent. Nope, it was littered with cheap ingredients such as cucumber handroll and tamago and cheap salad. \n\nI'm actually quite bummed that this was the most expensive yet most horrible one in Ho Chi Minh so far. Save your money, you'll be better off eating street food.\n\nOh, and those of you who actually \"think\" La Phong's ingredients are fresh? I seriously think you need to raise your standards. Try *any * Japanese food anywhere else - Japan, Taiwan, Malaysia, Singapore, etc... it's definitely much better than this.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 26, 2015",
