            "review_text": "Damohan\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam59 contributions\n0\nFresh, authentic Japanese food\nSep 2015 • Solo\nI had lunch here today and opted for a lunch set - sashimi and breaded seafood - with some sushi orders on the side.\n\nThe toro (fatty tuna) sushi was absolutely excellent, one of the best I've ever had.\n\nThe lunch set was great, high quality tuna and salmon sashimi, with superbly cooked seafood - even the octopus, which I don't usually eat, was tender and tasty.\n\nThe set was large and good value at about 200,000vnd, especially as I enjoyed all of the sides which were very well put together.\n\nI sat at the sushi bar which seats about 10, and enjoyed watching the chefs work, although tables are available. The friendly and efficient staff were all Vietnamese, but I think the chefs were Japan-trained or have a Japanese boss as everything seemed very authentic.\n\nThe menu was extensive and definitely warrants further visits.\nRead more\nWritten September 17, 2015",
